<title>JAPAN: Japan asks U.S. for more air talks in early June.</title>
<headline>Japan asks U.S. for more air talks in early June.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Transport Ministry said on Monday it had asked the United States for formal bilateral talks in their civil aviation dispute to be held sometime in the first two weeks of June in Tokyo.</p>
<p>A ministry official said, however, that it was not yet clear whether the United States would agree.</p>
<p>U.S. and Japanese officials have been meeting irregularly on an informal basis this year to try to resolve problems in their current air pact and set the stage for talks on a more liberal accord.</p>
</text>
